{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Elohim came to Abimelech.</b> In the manner stated regarding Laban (Genesis 31:24) and Balaam (Numbers 22:24) — concerning whom Scripture does not use at that point וַיֵּרָא אֵלָיו (\"and He appeared to him\") or מַרְאוֹת אֱלֹהִים (\"divine visions\") or דִּבּוּר (\"speech\"), as is used regarding the Patriarchs and the other prophets, as it says: בַּמַּרְאָה אֵלָיו אֶתְוַדָּע בַּחֲלוֹם אֲדַבֶּר בּוֹ (Numbers 12:6). For indeed the blessed El did not appear to them at all then, but a voice came to them speaking only." "<b>You shall die.</b> You are wasting away through the illness that has begun in you, <b>for YHWH has closed fast</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:54.170056846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}